      {
        "key": "c",
        "label": "(c)",
        "source": {
          "qp": 14,
          "ms": 13
        },
        "stem": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Describe how you would determine the genotype of an F2 fruit fly with a grey body and long wings.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 14
            }
          }
        ],
        "marks": 3,
        "topics": [
          {
            "ref": "16.2(4)",
            "role": "primary"
          }
        ],
        "markScheme": {
          "marks": 3,
          "instruction": null,
          "guidance": [],
          "points": [
            {
              "n": 1,
              "text": "<b>1 </b> carry out a test cross / cross with a double homozygous recessive fruit fly / cross with fly with black body and short wings <b>;</b>  <i>plus any </i><b><i>two</i></b><i> from: </i> <i> </i>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 2,
              "text": "<b>2</b>  if <b>some</b> offspring have black body then F2 fly is, heterozygous for the body colour (gene) / <b>Aa ; </b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 3,
              "text": "<b>3</b>  if <b>all</b> offspring have grey body then F2 fly is, homozygous dominant for body colour (gene) / <b>AA ; </b> <b> </b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 4,
              "text": "<b>4</b>  if <b>some</b> offspring have short wings then F2 fly is, heterozygous for wing length (gene) / <b>Bb ; </b> <b> </b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 5,
              "text": "<b>5</b>  if <b>all</b> offspring have long wings then F2 fly is, homozygous dominant for wing length (gene) / <b>BB ;</b><i> </i>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            }
          ]
        },
        "er": [],
        "aiSupplement": {
          "explanation": [
            {
              "text": "A homozygous recessive tester supplies only recessive alleles. Offspring phenotypes can then reveal alleles masked by dominance in the individual being tested.",
              "refs": [
                "syllabus:16.2(4)",
                "ms:c#1"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reasoningChain": [
            "Choose a suitable recessive tester.",
            "Relate each possible offspring class to an allele in the tested parent."
          ],
          "inferredMistakes": [
            {
              "text": "Using a homozygous dominant individual as the tester",
              "basis": "inferred",
              "refs": [
                "syllabus:16.2(4)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "type": "short"
